  "coordinates": "Full-slide level-0 pixels, origin at top-left. Rectangles and single brush strokes keep their original geometry. A compound region starts with an optional base rectangle followed by strokes in order. Paint and outline add round-capped, round-joined centerlines of the specified diameter. Erase subtracts the same footprint only from this region. Fill closes the point sequence, adds its even-odd polygon interior and strokes its closed boundary. Clip the result to the slide extent.",
  "certainty_default": "high",
  "change_note": "Evidence regions support multiple paint and erase strokes, connected outlines, and explicit polygon closure and fill.",
